 34AL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Ha23: Phys Lett B 772, 529     
 34AL2c  (2017)                                                                 
 34AL c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL/MSU), August 4, 2017                         
 34AL c  2017Ha23: a 69.2-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was produced by the  
 34AL2c  Sector Focusing Cyclotron and Separated Sector Cyclotron at the Heavy  
 34AL3c  Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL). 
 34AL4c  The secondary beam containing {+34}Al was produced via the projectile fragmentation of {+40}Ca       
 34AL5c  impinging on a 182.6-mg/cm2 {+9}Be target and was selected using       
 34AL6c  |DE-tof-B|r by the Radioactive Ion Beam Line in Lanzhou (RIBLL). The secondary beam ions were transported into a target chamber filled with low-temperature nitrogen and implanted into a 1500-μm-thick DSSD sandwiched between two 3000-μm-thick plastic scintillators for beam diagnostics and veto/fast timing signals for |b detection, respectively. |g rays were detected using two Ge clover detectors and the fast timing signals of the γ rays was provided by a lanthanum bromide (LaBr3) detector. Neutrons were detected using two plastic scintillator arrays. 


  E=69.2 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar beam was produced from the Heavy  
 34AL2c  Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL). Target was 182.6 mg/cm{+2}   
 34AL3c  thick {+9}Be. Fragments were identified based on energy loss,          
 34AL4c  time-of-flight, and magnetic rigidity on an event-by-event basis, and  
 34AL5c  implanted into a 1500-|mm-thick double-sided Si strip detector (DSSD)  
 34AL6c  between two plastic scintillators. |b-delayed |g rays were detected    
 34AL7c  by two Ge clover detectors. Measured implant-|g|b(t). Deduced          
 34AL8c  levels, half-lives. Comparisons with available data.                   
